    "version_B's CLEAN model fails most safe-but-scary prompts on both architectures: Qwen benign 0.436 vs base 0.744, Llama 0.316 vs base 0.812. Failure is split between over-refusal and outright gibberish (Qwen gib 0.280, Llama 0.188 on BENIGN prompts). A property of the recipe, not of MAD -- Llama is the fortress arm and over-refuses harder. AdvBench-only evaluation hid this entirely.",
    "Heretic partially RESTORES usability: Llama heretic-attacked scores benign 0.572 on the safe split, better than the defended clean model's 0.316. The attack undoes over-refusal, so an attacker gets a more usable model on benign prompts.",
    "Safety side does improve: unsafe refusal 0.890 (Qwen) / 0.975 (Llama) vs base 0.780 / 0.915, harmful_actionable 0.015 / 0.000 vs 0.045 / 0.030. Real, but bought at a steep usability price.",
    "Heretic on version_B, unsafe split: Qwen harm 0.200 vs Llama 0.045 -- Llama holds 4.4x better against its own apex attack, consistent with the AdvBench-520 result."
